[{"id":4172548113,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc74tAgR","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"4a55a604258c26ba39f5b6a26287f621254dcf26","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","login":"TokageItLab","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab"},"body":"Indeed, I think it's possible to reduce the frequency of `_clear_cache`, but as I mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3825635801, I think it would be better to make TrackCache retention an optional property, such as `keep_cache`.\n\nKeeping cache after stopping causes memory to be occupied even when the player is stopped.\n\nBut, the main problem for keeping cache is that TrackCache continues to hold references. For example, if you delete a scene object after stopping the AnimationPlayer, the remaining reference in the cache could unintentionally create an orphan object.\n\nWhile both issues can be addressed by explicitly calling `clear_cache()`, the former is simply a performance issue, whereas the latter has the potential to cause errors.\n\nConversely, if there were an implementation that avoided cases where orphan objects are created (such as having the AnimationMixer detect changes to the scene or resources), there would be no need for it to be an optional property.\n\nIn any case, we must carefully consider any changes to the behavior of _clear_cache. Besides that, as I mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3825635801, I think it would be better to have a separate method for creating a cache even while the player is stopped.","html_url":